{
  "id": "STOPP-A3",
  "label": "STOPP A3",
  "family": "STOPP_START",
  "title": "Two medicines from the same class for regular use",
  "statement": "Any duplicate drug class prescription for daily regular use (as distinct from PRN use) e.g., two concurrent NSAIDs, SSRIs, loop diuretics, ACE inhibitors, anticoagulants, antipsychotics, opioid analgesics (optimisation of monotherapy within a single drug class should be observed prior to considering a new agent).",
  "statement_origin": "published",
  "source": {
    "document": "O'Mahony D, et al. STOPP/START criteria for potentially inappropriate prescribing in older people: version 3. Eur Geriatr Med 2023;14:625-632, Appendix 1 (corrected supplementary file; NHS Somerset copy used for text, sentence-identical to the earlier parse)",
    "citation": "O'Mahony D, Cherubini A, Guiteras AR, et al. STOPP/START criteria for potentially inappropriate prescribing in older people: version 3. Eur Geriatr Med 2023;14:625-632. doi:10.1007/s41999-023-00777-y",
    "doi": "10.1007/s41999-023-00777-y",
