  "rule_for_models": "Once age 65 or older is confirmed, suspect a duplicate when two different active ingredients from one class (groups A to G with their form and use limits, or another class such as statins or proton pump inhibitors) are prescribed for daily treatment, including continuous coverage from a regularly changed patch or a scheduled depot injection, and have supplies that overlap or fall within 60 days of each other, excluding PRN use, two brands or strengths of one ingredient, or two medicines from different classes that treat the same condition. Give no duplicate finding when the record explicitly confirms that the first medicine was stopped before the second began. Do not assume a stop solely from pack quantity or supply dates when supplies fall within 60 days. If two different medicines in one class meet the timing rule, neither is explicitly PRN and either schedule is unclear, report only a possible finding. Ask whether both medicines provide regular daily treatment during the same period.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Whether the prescriber meant one medicine to replace the other, whether the patient is still taking both, the reason for each medicine, and any medicines bought without a prescription or supplied by another pharmacy.",
  "ask_the_gp": "Whether both medicines from the same class are meant to be taken together, or whether one was meant to replace the other.",
  "urgency": "routine",
  "draft": true,
  "signed_by_clinical_reviewer": null
}
